WEBVTT

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:09.690
Correct. The island is located right between the English/Scottish border.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.530
Now you will be able to see the island that the Scottish nobleman had ordered.

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:18.580
He ordered bullet-proof glass as an anti-terrorist measure,

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.710
But Japan is a peaceful country, so you might prefer stained-glass.

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.920
This island is artificial,

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:28.710
But you already own an island, which saves you some money.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.710
How about using stained-glass for the sunroof,

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.970
And mirrored glass for the walls?

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.470
Please have a look! We can see the island now...

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:40.970
Mr. Togo.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.110
This is our company's masterpiece: Ille to Boraraigh.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.110
Gaelic name from Norse meaning "Fort Island"

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:51.230
The Glass Fortress.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:16.300
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:27.650
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:39.410
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:45.710
The weak person I was is no more

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:51.290
I decided to just believe

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:58.430
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:02.260
I go towards you

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:09.980
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.110
I go towards you

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:18.150
Blown by the wind

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:23.620
Oh blown

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:32.590
The Glass Fortress

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.730
The blonde girl in the blue bikini,

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:54.360
Rosie Cox. That's the donor this time, eh Mr. Walton?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.860
Lively and beautiful.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.070
There is no shadow of her former pale and bony body. She's fine.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.370
Yeah...

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.040
She's quite the nymph.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:14.170
Hello Rosie! You've become quite well.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.590
It's all thanks to you, Mr. Walton.

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.550
I was addicted to heroin, but you remade me.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:23.140
It's all your own efforts, Rosie.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.680
Healthy lifestyle, food, exercise and rest...

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.890
All I did was provide these to you.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:31.850
Oh, no!

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:35.770
You also set me up with such a nice job.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:39.400
This is not your regular rehab center.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.990
Finding a good job for everyone to rehabilitate them...

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.030
This is our goal.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:48.080
I really appreciate it!

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:53.460
Now Rosie,

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.960
How about showing the gentleman how well you are now?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.340
Of course Mr. Walton!

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.630
What does Rosie know about me?

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:06.300
You are the greatest movie agent in the Philippines.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:12.810
You saw the movie she was an extra in, and have been trying to scout her ever since.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:17.610
I see. Then she will come with me willingly.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.490
Congratulations, Rosie.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.780
Your day of departure has come.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.270
What's wrong, Rosie?

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.520
Come here...

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.440
There's nothing to be scared of...

00:04:58.440 --> 00:04:59.570
Come on!

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:07.320
Rosie!

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:24.590
Woohoo!

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:29.600
I envy them, to be able to play around like that.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:33.350
It's been six months since we came to Manila,

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:37.770
Don't you miss our home in Belfast, Melinda?

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.070
Yes, a little bit, but...

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.650
Thankfully, it's easier to spend the winters here...

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.610
I didn't think I would make it through the last one.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:56.620
Did you hear what the doctor had to say about the heart transplant?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.750
Yes, however...

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.710
I feel like a monster putting someone else's organ in my body.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:07.470
It's too creepy for me, even thinking about it.

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.050
This is the forefront of medical science, Melinda.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:17.230
According to the doctor, most of the donors are male.

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:21.610
Their hearts are not suited to women like me.

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:31.370
If we could get a female donor, that would be ideal.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:36.160
Melinda. You will have that operation,

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:39.080
Even if it costs me my entire estate!

00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:40.460
Darling...

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:46.840
I am so happy, to be loved by a wonderful man like you.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:52.760
After our daughter Vanessa ran away, you are all that's left of my family.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:56.270
If you were to disappear, I would be all alone.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:02.650
It has been five years since she ran away...

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.320
I hope she's safe...

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:08.280
Ah, it's alright.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:13.070
They say no news is good news. I'm sure she's fine.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.120
That's true...

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.550
Sorry about the error Mr. Garciano.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:39.480
It seems that during the trip, the donor heard the story about the traffic in organs,

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.730
So she somehow escaped and jumped off the ship.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:47.980
And that is why the director of the hospital came to me in person?

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:51.200
I dealt with the Manila city police and media,

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:55.070
They believe an American tourist was killed in an accident.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:08:00.040
Don't worry about the donor. I'll send one next week to restock.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:05.250
I apologize. Please continue to work with us, Mr. Walton.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:11.380
The organs you provide are quite healthy. It's very reassuring.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:13.930
Female organs are particularly valuable!

00:08:13.930 --> 00:08:17.560
Well, consider it done, Director DeVilla.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:21.100
A helicopter?

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.940
Ah, I believe that's Dream Corporation's helicopter.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.730
This island is built by them.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:32.950
They asked if they could show it to a customer from Japan.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:37.120
He is supposedly interested in a similar villa.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.290
How can you be so relaxed?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:44.460
If our relationship is revealed, the secret of this island, we are done for!

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:49.920
Be at ease, they think this island is a resort.

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.550
It would be much more suspicious if I denied them.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:58.390
But I heard you were providing resources to anti-government terrorists!

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:03.430
Ah, sorry. But still...

00:09:03.890 --> 00:09:06.600
If you were to be shot from a helicopter!

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:10.900
With what just happened, it's better to lay low for a while-

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.900
That's not going to happen.

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:17.320
Right here is the safest place Mr. Walton could be.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:19.450
Allow me to explain:

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:32.050
The walls surrounding us are a specially formed triple-layer bullet-proof glass.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:37.930
From the ocean, a sonar system and glass protect him.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:42.180
From the sky, a glass roof protects him.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:46.810
But there is no glass roof over the pool!

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:53.190
If the resort were completely surrounded, the girls would find it very discomforting and stressful.

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:59.370
But then you cannot be perfectly safe, can you?

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.200
Then please look at this:

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:10.290
No matter which angle you take, the inside of the building cannot be targeted.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:17.220
J.J. is a professional shooter and Olympic Gold Medalist.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:21.550
It was J.J. who oversaw the construction of this island.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:29.560
As long as I remain here I am one-hundred percent safe Mr. DeVilla.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.190
But still...

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:38.110
Even if you take every possibility into account, you cannot be completely certain.

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.570
What do you mean?

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.070
What about ricochets?

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:43.580
Ricochets?

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:49.830
Yeah, even in a blind corner it's possible to ricochet a bullet into the building isn't it?

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.040
Is this true?

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:53.380
Yes...

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:55.840
Like a bank shot in billiards.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:59.840
You can shoot a bullet just like this.

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:07.100
Then in this case, you could glance a bullet off the water in the pool.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:09.140
Is that possible?

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.480
Yes, in theory...

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:18.440
However, even with my skill it is doubtful that this would work.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.200
However...

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:28.160
Even if the ricochet was pulled off, at best the bullet would hit the doorway, like this:

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:35.750
Even with a shot calculated by a computer, it is impossible to shoot Mr. Walton.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.760
I see, then it's perfect!

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:42.890
As long as you are here, old man, I'm at ease!

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:50.940
Have you seen enough, Mr. Togo?

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:53.350
Yes, thank you.

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:57.780
Impossible from the sea and the air...

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:02.490
It really is an impregnable glass fortress.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.520
Welcome to the island, Mr. Doherty.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:44.240
What a strict guard. Have you received a threat on Mr. Walton's life or anything similar?

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:50.240
Please excuse the inconvenience. We check all our guests.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.000
Protecting Mr. Walton is our job.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:57.080
His safety is our number one concern.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.270
Ah, it's you, Mr. Doherty!

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:18.770
This is your first time here, is it not?

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:23.820
When you asked about the donor coordinator, it was just a phone call.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.950
I heard that you never leave this island.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:32.290
There was no other way to see you in person.

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:36.290
Well, you came today to talk about your wife, Melinda, correct?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:43.920
Well, we found a donor, but an accident occurred during transportation. Please allow some more time.

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:50.390
I never imagined I would be dealing with Shylock!

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.180
Shylock?

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:58.980
The villainous moneylender from Shakespeare?

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:00.810
Is that how you see me?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:10.950
These girls are staying here without knowledge of your traffic. You are cultivating them like fishes!

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:13.160
Do you sympathize with them?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:18.210
From the very beginning the girls were as good as dead.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.710
Is it a crime to sell their organs?

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:24.000
Do you even have a conscience?!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:25.630
It's fine...

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:29.130
If it's a crime, I don't mind being called a criminal.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:33.640
You see, everyone commits crimes to live, don't they?

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.480
Just like Sisyphus from Greek mythology right?

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:36.480
Greek man who kept a dominant social position by killing travelers and guests.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:45.030
Now that my body is like this, without the girls, I would only have a few years to live.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:52.530
You yourself were interested in a donor girl for your wife's heart transplant, Mr. Doherty!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:59.290
That company's helicopter again...

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:07.670
Man, I'm beat. After painting this helicopter and flying here... you sure are a slave driver.

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:14.220
As soon as I finish your job and scrap this helicopter, I'm going back to America.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.440
Fly without talking. Right.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:22.690
Yes sir. You're paying me enough for it.

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.690
There are two targets.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.200
Vargas Walton and his right-hand man J.J.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:34.700
Walton is providing funding for international terrorist organizations.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.790
If we can't cut the terrorists' funding...

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:41.040
A disaster costing thousands of lives will happen.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.710
So... why me?

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:47.130
Because there is no proof...

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:52.550
On top of that, the island is an impregnable fortress.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:55.600
Other than the Grim Reaper, only you could reach him.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:00.350
Therefore, please! Accept this job.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.610
Please circle the island slowly.

00:16:10.150 --> 00:16:12.740
Of course, as you command.

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:18.330
Please look at this.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:29.050
This is...

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.510
Dear Mum and Dad, I hope that you have both been doing well.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:38.180
I am very sorry for being out of touch for such a long time.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:41.520
As you know, I left for London with aspirations of becoming an actress.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:48.070
I went through some cosmetic surgery and took the stage name Rosie Cox,  but sad to say that didn’t help land me any acting jobs.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:52.740
I had been so ashamed of myself of late, and could not gather the courage to face you guys.  I know you had high expectations...

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:59.830
However, Mr Walton - a real gentleman - took me to a beautiful rehab center made out of glass.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:03.830
He provided my rehabilitation, as well as an opportunity to work in a Filipino movie.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.210
I know its just a Filipino movie, but at least its an acting job...

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:12.260
When the first movie finishes shooting, I’ll go back home!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.970
I have enclosed a post-operation picture.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:19.140
Your loving daughter, Vanessa.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.020
Rosie Cox is my daughter!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.520
My daughter! Vanessa!

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:31.440
When her body was found in Manila Bay...

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.940
I didn't recognize it as Vanessa!

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:41.540
When I got to Belfast, the airmail had already been delivered.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.540
Can you understand how I felt?

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.540
If it is from child to parent, it should be a suitable donor indeed!

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:57.300
Choosing Vanessa when you aren't aware that they are parent and child...

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:01.560
It really proves your ability as a donor coordinator!

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:07.560
But in a way, I am glad that she died...

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:16.070
Otherwise my wife was about to have a heart transplant with a heart stolen from her own daughter!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:21.530
Just thinking about it is so terrible! Oh, cruel world!

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:32.500
Circle around... slowly.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:35.010
Just what are you going to do?

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:38.510
Those walls are triple-layered bullet-proof glass, right?

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:39.760
How will you-

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:45.100
Right. Shut up and fly.

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:48.600
Maintain this altitude and turn slowly please.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:51.100
Right right, as you command!

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.040
Wh- What are you going to do with me?

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:09.410
It's obvious!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:13.590
You!!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:18.510
You must not live!!!

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.180
J.J.!

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:34.190
As long as I'm on this island, nobody can kill Mr. Walton.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:40.320
When you see Death, why not ask him to get me, Mr. Doherty.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.750
Mr. Walton!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.220
Where?! Where did it come from?!

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:15.520
A ricochet? A ricochet got in here?!

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:19.190
You... how did you?

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:20.400
Circle again.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.530
As you command!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:29.450
B- But even with a computer to calculate it...

00:20:29.450 --> 00:20:31.580
How did he do it?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.710
That's it... the waves!

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:46.090
using the waves made by the girls, the angle of the ricochet can be changed!

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:48.220
But...

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:52.560
There is no human being capable of doing that.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:54.690
Luck...

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:57.060
It was a lucky shot!

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:06.490
I...

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.660
It wasn't..

00:21:09.080 --> 00:21:10.330
Lucky.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:10.450
Shot.

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.680
It.. It's a miracle!

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:29.180
A miracle from God!

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:48.570
You don't talk about the transplant anymore.

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:55.660
Even if I die tomorrow, I am happy enough...

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:59.540
Because I can die loved by you so much.

00:22:00.290 --> 00:22:03.630
If only I knew where Vanessa was now...

00:22:08.130 --> 00:22:09.550
It's okay,  Melinda.

00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:12.140
She is fine wherever she is.

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:14.520
No news is good news.

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:18.230
Yes... yes, that's right.

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:21.190
She is our daughter after all...

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:39.000
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:44.550
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.710 --> 00:22:53.430
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:55.770
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.770 --> 00:23:03.860
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:07.780
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:13.030
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:13.070 --> 00:23:21.250
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:25.840
It was just a dream

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:29.260
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:34.260
In this calm night

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.510
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:41.650
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:47.610
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:54.070
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:05.130
There is a lady earnestly waiting.

00:24:06.090 --> 00:24:13.260
She firmly believes her husband's murderer will come for her.

00:24:14.260 --> 00:24:16.550
On Malta Island:

00:24:16.550 --> 00:24:19.350
Golgo's merciless shot rings out.

00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:25.730
Melancholy Summer

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:22.020
Next time, on Golgo 13:

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:24.100
Melancholy Summer.

00:24:24.560 --> 00:24:26.730
Don't stand behind him...

00:24:26.730 --> 00:24:28.730
If you value your life.
